Wrap them behind an interface so you can swap in a fake during tests:

```csharp
public interface IFileSystem
{
    string ReadAllText(string path);
    void WriteAllText(string path, string contents);
    bool DirectoryExists(string path);
}

public class FileSystem : IFileSystem
{
    public string ReadAllText(string path) => File.ReadAllText(path);
    public void WriteAllText(string path, string contents) => File.WriteAllText(path, contents);
    public bool DirectoryExists(string path) => Directory.Exists(path);
}
```

Then inject `IFileSystem` into your classes instead of calling `File`/`Directory` directly. In tests, use a mock or a simple in-memory implementation.

Alternatively, **`System.IO.Abstractions`** (NuGet) provides a ready-made `IFileSystem` with an in-memory test helper (`MockFileSystem`), saving you from hand-rolling the wrapper.
